          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a note says \"use additional code\", is that optional?",
          "answer": "The retrieved passages don't say whether \"use additional code\" is optional, so I can't answer that directly.\n\nWhat they do say comes from the document \"ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection.\" It describes \"code first\" and \"use additional code\" as a pair that fixes the order of codes: the underlying condition is reported before its manifestation. It separately describes \"code also,\" which means two codes are needed but doesn't set an order. The same document notes that where a combination code exists, it is used instead of separate codes.\n\nFor the rule itself, check the official ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting, or ask a certified medical coder. This is a coding question, so a clinician is not the right person unless the question is about a specific patient's record.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
